      "task_id": "T3_002",
      "condition": "evolving",
      "function": "transpose_rows",
      "source": "def transpose_rows(rows):\n    \"\"\"\n    Transpose a rectangular list of lists.\n    \n    Args:\n    rows: A list of lists representing a rectangular matrix.\n    \n    Returns:\n    A new list of lists representing the transposed matrix.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Check if the input is empty\n    if not rows:\n        return []\n    \n    # Get the number of columns in the original matrix\n    num_columns = len(rows[0])\n    \n    # Initialize an empty list to store the transposed matrix\n    transposed_matrix = [[] for _ in range(num_columns)]\n    \n    # Iterate over each row in the original matrix\n    for row in rows:\n        # Iterate over each element in the current row\n        for i, value in enumerate(row):\n            # Add the element to the corresponding column in the transposed matrix\n            transposed_matrix[i].append(value)\n    \n    return transposed_matrix",
