      "source": "def longest_zero_run(values):\n    # Initialize variables to keep track of the current run and the maximum run found\n    current_run = 0\n    max_run = 0\n    \n    # Iterate through the values list\n    for value in values:\n        # If the current value is zero, increment the current run\n        if value == 0:\n            current_run += 1\n            # Update the maximum run if the current run is greater\n            if current_run > max_run:\n                max_run = current_run\n        else:\n            # Reset the current run to zero if the current value is not zero\n            current_run = 0\n    \n    # Return the maximum run found\n    return max_run\n\n# Example usage\nvalues = [1, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1, 0]\nprint(longest_zero_run(values))  # Output: 3",
